# wavefront_compact.ckir - CEIR-19c STAGE 2 (the WAVEFRONT): the SERIAL stream-compaction kernel. Scans N=8 hit-flags and
# writes the DENSE list of hit indices (compacted) + the hit count. AUTHORED (mandate #1: NO C++ builder; the .ckir is the
# SOLE source, edited DIRECTLY). BRANCHLESS: unconditional store compacted[cursor]=i, then cursor += flag[i] (0/1) — a miss's
# tentative write is overwritten by the next hit or sits harmlessly beyond count (no inner If => no if-block-shared-temp scar).
# local_size=1 (ONE thread => serial deterministic, no race, no tid guard; the fixed queue order the §134 GPU==oracle
# bit-exactness rests on). BINDING CONTRACT: TLAS@0 (DEAD — the bridge's rt.ray_query needs a %tlas operand at descriptor 0 +
# the AccelStructDecl forces #version 460; the compact NEVER traces), hit_flags@1 (read, N u32), compacted@2 (write, N u32),
# count@3 (write, 1 u32). The 18a per-workgroup prefix-sum is a PERF follow-up. The [[ext]] pool sections round-trip (19c fix).
schema = 1

